#import "../lib.typ": *

#runhead("Final Thoughts")

#chapter[Final Thoughts]
Elders and Sisters,

Wow, what a ride it\'s been! It’s been real. Putting this guide together for you has been both a challenge and a joy, much like learning Serbian and Croatian. It\'s far from perfect, but I hope it becomes a trusty sidekick as you navigate the twists and turns of mastering this beautiful language.

I wish I could magically transfer all my language knowledge to you in an instant, making your mission a breeze. But we both know that\'s not how growth happens. Learning a new language is tough. There are days when it feels like you\'re scaling a mountain in flip flops, when the words just won\'t stick, and frustration threatens to take over. On those days, remember why you started. Remember that your Heavenly Father believes in your ability to succeed, and so do I.

There\'s a quote that\'s been on my mind lately: \"Sometimes we admire things like the stars or a sunset. We love them, but deep down we know they won\'t last forever, and we can never quite reach them.\" Learning a language isn\'t like that. It\'s not some distant dream. With persistence and a bit of grit, you\'ll get there. I have no doubt.

As we wrap up this chapter, I want you to know how proud I am of each of you. If you\'ve made it this far, if you\'ve pushed through the tough days and celebrated the small victories, then you\'re already succeeding. Keep going. Keep pushing boundaries. Keep embracing the challenges because they\'re shaping you into the incredible missionaries you are.

I\'m excited to hear about your adventures after the mission. Drop me a message sometime and let me know how you\'re doing. Especially if you finish this whole freaking pdf. I’m always down to meet up and hangout. Whether our paths cross again soon or not, I look forward to catching up in heaven one day.

Stay awesome, Elders and Sisters. Keep killing it. Hurrah for Israel!

Best of luck,

Starešina Levi Mackay

